-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled and resolved dependencies
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This product resolves most of its dependencies from Maven and bundles the rest
under lib/. THIRD-PARTY.md lists both, and is regenerated by
`./gradlew licenseReport` from each artifact's published POM.

Two things it records rather than resolves. Eight artifacts publish no licence
in their POM, the OpenJFX ones among them. And the jars committed under lib/
have no Maven artifact and no machine-readable metadata; several are
version-stripped and predate the practice of shipping a licence inside the jar,
so each needs a human answer.

Both matter because shadowJar merges everything into one distributed uber-jar,
where a copyleft component affects redistribution of that artifact. The report
shows several: JRuby (GPL-2.0/LGPL-2.1/EPL-2.0, via AsciidoctorJ), JediTerm
(LGPL 3.0), JNA (LGPL-2.1-or-later or Apache-2.0), logback and pty4j (EPL).
